            "review_text": "aerofaze\nColorado Springs, Colorado493 contributions\n0\nComfort soup at its best\nSep 2014 • Friends\nGood northern-style pho at a local's joint!\n\nThere were four of us that morning. No sooner had I placed my order that my delicious bowl of pho arrived. Though fewer condiments are provided compared to other pho establishments that you might be used to, they let the heady, rich broth do the talking. It wasn't as hot (temperature-wise) as I wanted, but other than that it was pretty darn close to greatness. I love pho and this bowl certainly satisfied my craving for it.\n\nThe interior is simple, but the decor lent a nice touch. French-style street lamps warmed up the concrete floor, and the wooden slatted chairs matched the wall art displaying Hanoi's street scenes.\n\nPrices were very affordable and service was pretty quick. They had a steady stream of comings and goings, but that morning there were no tourists to be seen... well, except for my husband and me.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 16, 2014",
